GRADING DECISIONS AND EDGE-CASE RETENTION
88: Numeric degrees from the seal; h cancels both degree-eight terms and retains degree 2.
89_and_97: Natural Boolean answers have no supplied proven input contract. Keep full ungraded decisions; do not invent 1/0 coding or exact-string exclusivity.
90: Any two distinct legitimate solutions remain acceptable. Complete example answers are displayed, with no fixed-example automatic rejection of other pairs.
91: Full proofs are displayed; point or empty-set keys do not replace proof requirements.
92_through_95: Full constructions and all solution sets are displayed, not sample-only plots. No image work is claimed.
95_f: Precisely {(0,0)}; no positive-radius circle, disk, or additional point.
96_and_98: Fixed x^2+y^2= left side is declared in each part label; numeric right sides encode the requested circle equations. Full equations remain displayed.
99: x is expressed using y. a/b cover every real y in the fixed labels and full display. c has forbidden y=-1 and F(-1)=empty; d has forbidden y=2 and F(2)=empty. Exceptional values are separately numeric-graded; neither empty fiber is dropped or made a free-x fiber.
100: a retains forbidden values -1 and 7, including the canceled-factor hole; b retains forbidden -7 and allows both numerator zeros. Formula equivalence alone is not used to silently fill original holes.
101: Complete intervals, union, all-real set, and empty set are displayed. No supplied proven full-set input contract; do not judge only endpoints or invent exact keys.
ungraded_is_not_HOLD: Every ungraded item has its complete sealed requested result. Contract or task-type limitations, not absent mathematical results, explain ungraded.
auto_is_candidate_only: The numeric/expression decomposition is an author choice for reliable quantity comparison; no runtime or parser contract execution is claimed in this restricted author turn.

